# THE FOUR-TOWN RUN CONTINUED FROM 175,000 WITH THE EXPLORE BONUS AT 100 M (user 2026-11-15: "how about big
# return for explore mode is at 100m", and on my proposal of a fresh run: "its should bd a resume").
# = slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_lc01_miss_fault10_resume_warm_par.env (job 466568: fault
#   charge 10, resume warm-up 15,000) with ONLY:
#   EXPLORE_GOAL_DIST_M=100 instead of 200: an explore episode is paid EXPLORE_ARRIVAL_BONUS (+100) and ends as
#   "reached" once it is 100 m from its start in a straight line (EXPLORE_DIST_MODE=net).
# WHY: explore episodes average 65-75 m in training, so the +100 at 200 m is rarely collected; at 100 m it is
#   collected often and pays directly for driving on without a fault (metres per fault have sat at 65-85 m
#   since 25,000 decisions).
# WHAT IT COSTS: training no longer contains explore drives beyond 100 m from the start. The critic's
#   explore-progress input (distance toward the bonus as a fraction) now reaches 1 at 100 m, not 200 m, so the
#   resumed critic reads that input on a new scale and has to relearn it.
# KNOWN RISK, NOT SOLVED: every resume of this run so far lost ground once the actor was updated on the fresh
#   replay (466554, 466557; 466568 with the warm-up held the old level for 15,000 decisions and began to slide
#   within 2,500 of the release: temperature 0.089 -> 0.106, 77 -> 56 m per fault). This run can show the same.
# Start with FRL_RESUME=<frl_c0actor_priv_4towns_lc01_miss_2m>/step_175000 under a NEW run name.
. "$REPO/slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_lc01_miss_fault10_resume_warm_par.env"
export EXPLORE_GOAL_DIST_M=100
